# Review ownership. GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a
# pull request touches.
#
# The branch ruleset does not require a code-owner review
# (require_code_owner_review is false), so these are requests, not gates. They
# exist so a change lands in front of someone who knows the area rather than
# waiting to be noticed.

# Everything, unless a more specific rule below wins.
*                           @ciscokwiz

# The signing path. These files decide what bytes get signed, so a change here
# is the one most worth a second pair of eyes.
/preimage.go                @ciscokwiz
/signer.go                  @ciscokwiz
/authorize.go               @ciscokwiz
/delegates.go               @ciscokwiz
/verify.go                  @ciscokwiz

# The correctness gate. A change to the generator or the committed vectors
# changes what "proven" means for the whole library.
/testdata/gen/              @ciscokwiz
/testdata/vectors/          @ciscokwiz
/golden_test.go             @ciscokwiz

# CI and the branch ruleset's required checks.
/.github/                   @ciscokwiz

# The build brief. Not to be modified; ownership here makes an attempt visible.
/CLAUDE.md                  @ciscokwiz
